No, it comes from High Culture. To be specific, Gilbert & Sullivan's _The
Mikado_ , where it is the executioner's sword belonging to Ko-Ko, the Lord
High Executioner of Titipu. I wonder whether it shouldn't occasionally
attack its wearer, since Ko-Ko was also the first criminal condemned to
die by the sword in Titipu.
